Process's per-platform members for WitOS (plan step N4.2, RFC 0015 section 8), as Process.FreeBSD.cs holds FreeBSD's:
a process starts through the libc's posix_spawn over the process manager and ends as waitpid reports, and what Linux
reads from /proc — the start time, another process's processor times, the parent, the working set, the affinity —
is PlatformNotSupportedException, since WitOS has no /proc and the kernel reports none of it.

--- a/src/libraries/System.Diagnostics.Process/src/System/Diagnostics/Process.WitOS.cs
